Bandit Level 12 - Level 13

Challenge: Repeatedly decompress a file.

Solution:

mktemp -d - create temp directory
cp -t /tmp /tmp.qUByq2Xe3X data.txt - copy file into temp dir
cd /tmp /tmp.qUByq2Xe3X - move into temp dir
mv data.txt file1 - change name of file
xxd -r file1 > file2 - reverse the hexadecimal dump back into its original binary data.
file file2 - find decompression of first file

Continue using:
ss
gzip -d (file-name).gz
bzip2 -d (file-name).bz
tar -xf (file-name).tar

after every decompression use ls to find the new file created
then use file (file name) to find the new decompression

all the way until you reach the final text file.

Explanation:

Use file to identify the file type after each extraction.
Decompress repeatedly until you reach the final text file.

